      "message": "I meant to delete this, as its increased in `testcase.yaml`. In tests `fingerprint.task.capture` and `fingerprint.task.template` you\u0027ll get these failures\n\n```\n[00:00:00.710,000] \u003cwrn\u003e test_host_command: requested response size 25608 exceeds Host Command TX buffer size 544. Truncating.\nec:~\u003e [00:00:00.710,000] \u003cinf\u003e host_cmd_handler: HC 0x0404\n[00:00:00.710,000] \u003cinf\u003e host_cmd_handler: HC 0x0404\nec:~\u003e [00:00:00.710,000] \u003cinf\u003e host_cmd_handler: HC 0x0404 err 3\n[00:00:00.710,000] \u003cinf\u003e host_cmd_handler: HC 0x0404 err 3\nec:~\u003e \n    Assertion failed at CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR/src/fpsensor_capture.cc:326: fpsensor_capture_test_finger_capture_simple_image_scan_success_get_frame: ec_cmd_fp_frame(NULL, \u0026frame_request, frame_buffer) is non-zero\n```\n\nIncreasing the buffer allows the entire response to be `memcpy` in `pass_args_to_sim` function. Otherwise the test hangs, as memory corruption occurs. This seems only related to `ec_host_cmd_backend_sim_install_send_cb` as it uses the tx_buf defined in the simulator for populating the response.",
